{"seq":1,"at":"2026-09-17","kind":"imported","target":{"type":"article","id":"a0902"},"reason":"Article of the Quiztopia bank (written for card c076): researched and transcribed in September 2026, converted to the quiz platform on 2026-10-20.","by":"Quiztopia import","ref":"quiz-archive/transcripts/quiztopia/c076.json"},
{"seq":2,"at":"2026-10-20","kind":"edited","target":{"type":"article","id":"a0902"},"reason":"Rewritten by the merge to take in the printed cards' questions.","by":"merge literature/classics","ref":"quiz-archive/runs/tp-ingest/decisions/zz-r2-literature__classics.json","changes":[{"field":"bodyEn","diff":[["=",84],["+","Its roots go back much further: in Frankfurt between about 1772 and 1775 the young Goethe wrote an early version, the so-called Urfaust, on which the finished Faust is built. He read it aloud in Weimar but never printed it; it survived only in a copy made by the court lady Luise von Göchhausen, which the scholar Erich Schmidt discovered and published in 1887 – proof that the Urfaust was the work of Johann Wolfgang von Goethe himself, not of his friend Johann Gottfried Herder. "],["=",1095]]},{"field":"bodyDe","diff":[["=",74],["+","Seine Wurzeln reichen viel weiter zurück: In Frankfurt schrieb der junge Goethe zwischen etwa 1772 und 1775 eine Frühfassung, den sogenannten Urfaust, auf dem der vollendete Faust aufbaut. Er las ihn in Weimar vor, ließ ihn aber nie drucken; erhalten blieb er nur in einer Abschrift der Hofdame Luise von Göchhausen, die der Germanist Erich Schmidt 1887 entdeckte und veröffentlichte – der Beweis, dass der Urfaust das Werk von Johann Wolfgang von Goethe selbst war und nicht seines Freundes Johann Gottfried Herder. "],["=",1081]]}]},
{"seq":3,"at":"2026-10-21","kind":"corrected","target":{"type":"article","id":"a0902"},"reason":"a0902 body: removed \"– proof that the Urfaust was the work of Johann Wolfgang von Goethe himself, not of his friend Johann Gottfried Herder\" (EN+DE) — the Göchhausen copy proves no such thing, and no one credits Herder with the Urfaust; the Urfaust sentence now reads \"the so-called Urfaust … was written by the young Johann Wolfgang von Goethe in Frankfurt between about 1772 and 1775\" and the opening sentence says just \"Goethe\" — https://de.wikipedia.org/wiki/Urfaust","by":"enrich batch 107","ref":"quiz-archive/runs/tp-enrich/enrich-report/a0458-a1418.md","sources":[{"url":"https://de.wikipedia.org/wiki/Urfaust"}]},
